#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""chat-build — build CLI for demo-chat.

A declarative replacement for build-app.sh + run-*.sh. Every backend, transport
and discovery mode is a Feature: a mapping from one CLI flag to Maven profiles,
Spring properties and JVM flags. The CLI resolves the requested features against
a Service definition, composes JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS in the same order build-app.sh
does, writes an env file, and runs Maven.

    chat-build core --memory --run --notls --key-type long
    chat-build core --kafka --build --notls --uuid
    chat-build rest --run --notls --key-type long --dry-run

The module is chat-deploy for client-shaped services, chat-authorization-server
for authserv, and chat-deploy-<backend> when a backend names its own composition
root. Backends used to be Maven profiles on chat-deploy that pulled their deploy
module in; that direction, plus the module's own dependency back on chat-deploy,
formed a reactor cycle.

Python 3.10+ stdlib only.
"""

